    "code": "def solution():\n    # Define variables\n    advertising_expenditure = [3000, 4000, 5000, 6000, 7000]\n    revenue = [20000, 23000, 25000, 26000, 28000]\n\n    # Calculate the least squares regression slope\n    mean_x = sum(advertising_expenditure) / len(advertising_expenditure)\n    mean_y = sum(revenue) / len(revenue)\n\n    numerator = sum(\n        (x - mean_x) * (y - mean_y)\n        for x, y in zip(advertising_expenditure, revenue)\n    )\n    denominator = sum(\n        (x - mean_x) ** 2\n        for x in advertising_expenditure\n    )\n\n    slope = numerator / denominator\n\n    # Return the slope rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(slope, 2)\n"
